WEBVTT

00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:08.294
Welcome to vNAAATS. In this video you will learn how to use CPDLC in the flight data display.

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:10.278
Signing into your station.

00:00:10.598 --> 00:00:15.622
Accepting pilots, sending level messages, and handling clearance requests.

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:18.406
Please note

00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:24.934
This is a demonstration using sample flights. It is not a live version of the FDD.

00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:32.230
Open the CPDLC window from the button at the top of the FDD.

00:00:32.646 --> 00:00:40.134
Sign in to your station using your own Hoppie code. You can tick the box to remember the code on this computer only.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.694
The server never stores it.

00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:47.142
Pilots who are close to oceanic airspace log on to your station.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.478
Auto except switched on.

00:00:50.086 --> 00:00:54.918
appear in the connected list by themselves, with how long they have been connected.

00:00:55.398 --> 00:00:59.910
A flashing call sign means a new message or a new logon.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.686
call sign to read the conversation with that pilot.

00:01:04.166 --> 00:01:06.022
The last 10 messages are shown.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:07.430
newest at the bottom.

00:01:07.878 --> 00:01:09.894
Automatic messages show here too.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.806
when a pilot reaches the oceanic entry point.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:18.214
They are sent a message confirming CPDLC contact with Gander or Shanwick.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:19.782
and they answer Roger.

00:01:20.358 --> 00:01:24.006
Crossing 30 west on NatFSS sends a second one.

00:01:24.646 --> 00:01:29.350
The pilot has not answered after three minutes. The message is tagged no reply.

00:01:30.182 --> 00:01:35.110
For a level change, choose climb, descend, maintain, or expect climb.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.838
then click the flight level.

00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:40.614
With send on click ticked, the message goes straight away.

00:01:41.286 --> 00:01:43.846
ticket if you would rather check the message first.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:54.246
For anything else, use the contact and squawk buttons, the quick replies, or the other row with resume normal speed and contact by voice.

00:01:54.662 --> 00:01:57.350
You can also pick one of the standard messages.

00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:00.422
text if you need to, then press send.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:05.862
Pilots can also ask for an oceanic clearance by CPDLC.

00:02:06.214 --> 00:02:09.510
though CPDLC is optional on VATSIM.

00:02:10.054 --> 00:02:12.806
pilots without it use natTrak as before.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.422
These requests appear in a list at the top of the window.

00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:18.054
with the level Mach.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:19.270
an M.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.574
the MAX FL the pilot gave.

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:25.158
They are marked in red when they are not yet in that track.

00:02:25.798 --> 00:02:27.526
The pilot is told at once.

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:31.206
RCL received by CZQO.

00:02:32.006 --> 00:02:35.622
EGGX depending on the area they enter.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.758
We cover how to answer them in the natTrak video.

00:02:39.878 --> 00:02:41.894
your pilot is leaving your frequency.

00:02:42.214 --> 00:02:43.558
Use UNIcon.

00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:47.654
This sends a CPDLC message to the pilot.

00:02:47.974 --> 00:02:50.310
telling them your services are terminated.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:56.454
and to monitor advisory or UNI-COM on 122.800.

00:02:56.806 --> 00:03:03.142
Once the pilot replies to the message, the tag in EuroScope will automatically untrack for you.

00:03:03.622 --> 00:03:05.862
You can also use log off pilot.

00:03:06.278 --> 00:03:07.718
if your station is stuck.

00:03:08.294 --> 00:03:10.566
and more and choose Force Logout.

00:03:11.014 --> 00:03:13.510
only after checking with the other controller.

00:03:14.246 --> 00:03:17.478
to UCPDLC on a second screen.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:24.422
The window opens on its own and carries on working while you use the main display.

00:03:25.158 --> 00:03:27.206
That is CPDLC.

00:03:27.622 --> 00:03:31.654
In the next video we cover how to use natTrak through the FDD.

00:03:32.006 --> 00:03:33.306
Thanks for watching.

